cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Okur, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Okur: a small, open Turkish text-to-speech model that runs in the browser"
abstract: >-
  A 9.8 M-parameter Turkish text-to-speech model (6.8 M acoustic model, 3.0 M decoder) trained from scratch on
  298 hours of openly licensed speech. A Rust/WebAssembly text frontend spells out numbers, reads ordinals and restores
  circumflexes; a flow-matching DiT distilled to 4 steps with DMD2 generates 25 Hz latents decoded to 48 kHz audio.
authors:
  - family-names: "Beşel"
    given-names: "Ahmet Hakan"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-09"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ahmethakanbesel/okur-tts"
url: "https://huggingface.co/spaces/ahakan/okur-tts"
keywords:
  - text-to-speech
  - Turkish
  - flow matching
  - DMD2
  - WebAssembly
